WEBVTT

00:23.870 --> 00:31.010
In an empty world, I recall the day which I cannot recover from.

00:31.550 --> 00:38.760
Smoke blows before my frozen fingertips.

00:39.220 --> 00:46.520
As I pursue memories that cannot be erased despite being soaked with rain,

00:46.940 --> 00:54.450
The shadow of time that is entangled in darkness acts as my key of pain.

00:55.700 --> 00:57.490
Find out

00:57.490 --> 01:00.540
Find out lost days

01:00.540 --> 01:02.910
For my life

01:16.220 --> 01:18.140
Key of Pain

01:20.470 --> 01:23.980
I'll find it out

01:24.100 --> 01:29.770
For your life

01:52.550 --> 01:53.090
Stop the car.

02:00.510 --> 02:01.350
Kuzuya-san.

02:21.530 --> 02:24.080
U-Um...

02:24.410 --> 02:25.830
Kagura-san...

02:25.830 --> 02:28.080
Were you planning to go in there?

02:29.420 --> 02:30.880
U-Um, well...

02:30.880 --> 02:33.710
I've been interested in that R&D lab, too.

02:35.460 --> 02:39.220
I saw a couple of strange men coming and going from there before.

02:39.220 --> 02:40.590
Strange men?

02:40.590 --> 02:41.510
Yeah.

02:41.510 --> 02:44.310
They were acting weird, so I tried looking into it once, but...

02:44.310 --> 02:44.970
Huh?

02:44.970 --> 02:45.560
That key...

02:46.140 --> 02:47.730
This is, um...

02:47.730 --> 02:49.310
Ren-kun!

02:49.310 --> 02:52.150
That's the key to the R&D lab, isn't it?

02:52.150 --> 02:53.060
Where did you find it?

02:53.060 --> 02:54.190
W-Well...

02:55.320 --> 02:57.570
Was it Kitagishi-san's office?

02:58.360 --> 02:59.820
I-I'm sorry!

02:59.820 --> 03:01.860
I'm really inquisitive, so, um...

03:01.860 --> 03:02.870
I'll put it back right now!

03:07.830 --> 03:09.540
Who are you?

03:29.140 --> 03:29.770
You're a detective?

03:31.390 --> 03:32.440
Yes.

03:32.440 --> 03:35.310
A client wants me to investigate Kitagishi-san.

03:35.310 --> 03:36.820
Kitagishi-san...

03:36.820 --> 03:38.070
Have you noticed any changes in his behavior?

03:38.610 --> 03:43.490
Now that you mention it, I saw him arguing with someone over the phone a few days ago.

03:43.950 --> 03:46.490
It didn't seem to be a normal conversation.

03:46.490 --> 03:47.990
Does that happen often?

03:48.370 --> 03:49.540
Well...

03:50.710 --> 03:51.960
Are you witness-interviewing me?

03:53.000 --> 03:53.830
It's okay.

03:53.830 --> 03:56.710
I'll help in any way I can.

03:56.710 --> 03:59.710
But in exchange, can you let me know what you find out?

04:00.340 --> 04:01.130
Kagura-san...

04:01.970 --> 04:04.050
A lot of strange things have been happening here...

04:04.050 --> 04:05.430
...and I've been wondering about them.

04:05.930 --> 04:09.600
Maybe if I know the reason why, it'll take a bit of the load off my mind.

04:09.600 --> 04:10.480
Okay.

04:17.150 --> 04:18.900
Can I take that as your agreement to our bargain then?

04:19.650 --> 04:20.440
Yes.

04:22.860 --> 04:23.740
What?

04:23.740 --> 04:24.740
"Matori"?

04:25.450 --> 04:27.030
Are you sure that's what the voice said?

04:27.030 --> 04:27.910
Yeah.

04:27.910 --> 04:29.310
The person knew about Kai, too.

04:29.310 --> 04:32.370
Pull him off this case immediately.

04:32.370 --> 04:33.540
Okay.

04:33.540 --> 04:36.040
I'll call an end to the undercover investigation for now.

04:36.750 --> 04:37.960
Get back to HQ.

04:39.500 --> 04:41.460
Is the key to Switch doing well?

04:43.510 --> 04:44.880
I...

04:45.930 --> 04:47.220
...will continue with the investigation.

04:47.220 --> 04:48.470
What the hell do you think you're saying?

04:48.470 --> 04:49.970
Something about it interests me.

04:50.560 --> 04:52.060
I'll trash my cell phone.

04:52.060 --> 04:54.020
If something happens, I'll contact you.

04:54.020 --> 04:54.770
Wait, Hal!

04:54.770 --> 04:55.480
Hey!

04:55.480 --> 04:56.850
Goddamnit!

04:58.940 --> 04:59.810
Resuming the investigation?

04:59.980 --> 05:00.940
Yeah.

05:00.940 --> 05:02.530
He's doing his own thing like he always does!

05:18.380 --> 05:19.210
Here it is.

05:19.210 --> 05:21.710
Do you see this strange mark after the number of plants received?

05:21.710 --> 05:26.760
I bet there's a large difference between the number written here and the number that was actually received on that day.

05:26.760 --> 05:29.050
Also, a large amount of it consists of rare species.

05:29.720 --> 05:31.890
These shipments come in over a fixed period.

05:31.890 --> 05:32.850
Yeah.

05:32.850 --> 05:36.310
All of them disappear into the R&D lab.
I haven't seen any put on exhibition.

05:36.640 --> 05:40.480
What's more, every time those shipments arrive, so do those strange men that I'd mentioned.

05:41.190 --> 05:47.490
Whenever they're here, Kitagishi-san would kick out the other researchers on staff for some reason or other.

05:47.490 --> 05:49.160
What in the world could be happening inside?

05:49.160 --> 05:53.450
To be honest, I tried to sneak into the lab myself once, because I wanted to know, too.

05:54.250 --> 05:57.120
But I couldn't open a single door.

05:57.120 --> 05:59.290
I guess I have no skill at picking locks.

05:59.290 --> 06:00.500
Oh, no...

06:00.500 --> 06:02.670
Where did you find that key?

06:02.670 --> 06:03.710
Oh, this?

06:04.340 --> 06:06.550
Inside that trick box.

06:06.550 --> 06:07.840
Trick box?

06:07.840 --> 06:09.390
I thought it was just an art piece.

06:10.510 --> 06:13.760
Kitagishi-san doesn't leave data in his computer...

06:13.760 --> 06:18.440
...but maybe we can find some kind of illegal evidence at the R&D lab.

06:18.440 --> 06:19.400
I agree.

06:19.400 --> 06:19.900
Let's go.

06:20.310 --> 06:22.690
But I don't think going there right now is a good idea.

06:22.690 --> 06:26.070
Kitagishi-san works late, so he should be coming back here soon.

06:26.990 --> 06:28.780
Let's put the key back in its place.

06:28.780 --> 06:30.360
We don't want him to get suspicious.

06:30.360 --> 06:31.240
You're right.

06:32.450 --> 06:34.120
Did you find anything else?

06:34.120 --> 06:34.910
Anything else?

06:37.160 --> 06:38.660
N-No.

06:38.660 --> 06:39.540
Not in particular.

06:39.540 --> 06:40.250
Okay.

06:42.790 --> 06:43.790
Blood?

06:45.550 --> 06:47.170
It's stopped snowing.

06:47.170 --> 06:48.920
But it's still cold.

06:49.380 --> 06:51.970
Everyone has the night off tomorrow.

06:52.430 --> 06:56.640
We should wait until then to go to the R&D lab.

06:56.640 --> 06:58.850
Thank you for telling me so much.

06:59.390 --> 07:00.390
That's okay.

07:00.390 --> 07:04.400
If the plants really are being used for crime, I could never allow that to happen.

07:04.400 --> 07:09.780
Besides, it makes me happy to be able to help someone as brave as you for trying to expose that all on your own.

07:09.780 --> 07:10.860
Oh, no...

07:10.860 --> 07:12.280
I'm not brave at all.

07:12.280 --> 07:13.660
I always keep dragging the others down.

07:14.780 --> 07:15.700
Ren-kun?

07:17.410 --> 07:19.790
That's what my partner always tells me.

07:19.790 --> 07:22.750
If I tell him that you've helped me this time,

07:22.750 --> 07:24.170
I'm sure he'll get mad again.

07:24.630 --> 07:27.840
I can just hear him yelling about how I can't do my own work by myself.

07:27.840 --> 07:30.680
Personally, I think it's a virtue to allow other people to help you.

07:30.680 --> 07:31.840
Kagura-san.

07:31.840 --> 07:35.140
Besides, I'm sure that despite what that person says,

07:35.140 --> 07:37.850
he really worries about you a lot.

07:38.470 --> 07:42.190
If you were someone he didn't care about,
he'd just ignore you without saying anything.

07:42.190 --> 07:43.230
Maybe...

07:43.230 --> 07:45.940
Don't you worry about him, too?

07:47.020 --> 07:48.860
I worry about him a lot!

07:51.610 --> 07:54.530
People don't spend time worrying about those they hate.

07:54.530 --> 07:56.780
No matter how many times he gets angry at you...

07:56.780 --> 07:58.040
...you still like him.

08:02.160 --> 08:03.750
Who did you call on the phone?

08:04.920 --> 08:06.500
That's none of your business.

08:10.970 --> 08:12.970
Is it something you can't tell me?

08:13.380 --> 08:17.100
Do I need your permission for making a single phone call?

08:19.270 --> 08:22.440
We know that you've been snooping around for something!

08:24.100 --> 08:26.610
Who do you trust more...

08:26.610 --> 08:28.150
...me or these incompetent goons?

08:42.460 --> 08:43.330
I see.

08:43.330 --> 08:47.000
First Criminal
Investigation Division

08:43.660 --> 08:46.210
The suspicious arrival of a large number of plants...

08:46.210 --> 08:46.960
...and...

08:48.130 --> 08:49.250
What is this?

08:49.630 --> 08:52.800
There's a disposal area inside the gardens that is specifically for plants,

08:52.800 --> 08:56.930
so it bugged me a little why something like that would be in his office trash bin.

08:56.930 --> 08:59.220
It looks like some kind of root.

08:59.220 --> 09:00.970
All right, I'll send it over to our expert substance analysts.

09:00.970 --> 09:01.680
Thank you.

09:02.060 --> 09:04.640
Also, about this man who provided you with information...

09:04.640 --> 09:06.100
Akito Kagura.

09:06.100 --> 09:08.480
He's a university student who works part-time at the botanical gardens.

09:08.900 --> 09:10.270
Can we trust what he said?

09:10.270 --> 09:13.990
I was able to check on the contents of Kitagishi-san's account books based on his testimony.

09:14.610 --> 09:15.650
I see.

09:15.650 --> 09:19.950
All that's left, then, is to investigate the non-admittance R&D lab.

09:19.950 --> 09:21.700
About Kitagishi...

09:21.990 --> 09:25.290
Apparently, he's gone M.I.A. since last night.

09:25.290 --> 09:29.500
I put another investigator on tailing Kitagishi at the same time you went undercover...

09:30.210 --> 09:32.710
...but he never returned home yesterday.

09:32.710 --> 09:34.470
Could he still be inside the gardens?

09:34.880 --> 09:36.510
I can't say.

09:36.510 --> 09:38.010
We're searching for him right now.

09:38.010 --> 09:40.260
If he hasn't left the gardens...

09:40.260 --> 09:42.060
...he'd be at...

09:42.060 --> 09:42.640
Director Hiki!

09:43.140 --> 09:45.850
I'll go investigate the R&D lab right now!

09:45.850 --> 09:47.650
Yeah, about that...

09:47.650 --> 09:50.440
We're thinking of suspending this undercover investigation for the time being.

09:51.020 --> 09:51.980
Why?

09:51.980 --> 09:54.990
Someone's figured out that we're investigating them.

09:56.320 --> 09:57.660
Then, what about Hal?

09:57.660 --> 09:58.990
Is Hal all right?

10:01.990 --> 10:03.790
We can't reach him.

10:05.370 --> 10:07.250
We can't make any careless calls, either.

10:07.250 --> 10:09.580
I've got men keeping a watch on Asaya's surroundings...

10:09.580 --> 10:11.750
...but we can't tell what's going on inside.

10:11.750 --> 10:12.960
No way...

10:12.960 --> 10:15.550
I believe Hal-kun is acting so of his own intent...

10:15.800 --> 10:18.340
...but his chances in this situation do not look optimistic.

10:19.010 --> 10:22.890
Then let's get a search warrant for Asaya and go in there!

10:22.890 --> 10:23.850
We have to save Hal!

10:23.850 --> 10:25.640
We have no hard evidence.

10:25.640 --> 10:28.100
Even if we've confirmed the place where F.A. is sold...

10:28.100 --> 10:31.440
...that doesn't necessarily mean it's being stored at Asaya's hideout.

10:31.860 --> 10:34.690
Kayama is one of Asaya's leaders!
What about his testimony?

10:34.690 --> 10:36.490
He didn't speak a word about it.

10:36.490 --> 10:40.030
If there was one person who could provide testimony against Asaya...

10:40.320 --> 10:42.410
...Hal-kun would be the only one.

10:42.410 --> 10:46.330
Now that Kitagishi, the only link we've got to Kuzuya, has gone missing, this whole thing is out of our hands.

10:48.250 --> 10:49.670
Kitagishi...

10:50.330 --> 10:52.380
Kitagishi just has to be found, right?

10:52.380 --> 10:52.960
What?

10:52.960 --> 10:53.840
Kai!

10:53.840 --> 10:54.380
Kaji-kun.

10:55.630 --> 10:57.210
There's something I need you to investigate for me right away.

10:58.800 --> 10:59.260
Sure.

11:12.190 --> 11:13.440
Reiji.

11:14.520 --> 11:17.560
Is this how you treat someone who very recently saved your life?

11:17.820 --> 11:19.820
It's your fault for not talking.

11:19.820 --> 11:21.950
I can't do that.

11:22.740 --> 11:23.410
Why?

11:24.740 --> 11:27.370
How much of a naïve sucker are you?

11:29.250 --> 11:30.410
What?

11:30.410 --> 11:32.710
You have a traitor lurking inside Asaya.

11:32.710 --> 11:37.550
He's been looking into the relationship between here and Kotetsu, and how F.A. is being manufactured...

11:37.550 --> 11:39.130
...so he can leak that info to the Matori.

11:39.880 --> 11:40.710
The Matori?

11:40.710 --> 11:43.090
I found a wiretap in your room.

11:43.090 --> 11:45.100
I can't determine who did it yet...

11:45.100 --> 11:48.270
...and in a situation where I don't even know who the traitor is...

11:48.270 --> 11:52.440
...do you honestly expect me to say in front of everyone that I'm looking for the traitor among us?

11:54.770 --> 11:58.480
The Matori are on guard about the upcoming exchange between Asaya and Kotetsu.

11:58.480 --> 12:02.430
They'll use whatever dirty means necessary to destroy both organizations.

12:03.070 --> 12:04.240
If you still don't trust me...

12:04.950 --> 12:06.580
...then kill me right now.

12:26.180 --> 12:27.350
Yesterday...

12:27.640 --> 12:31.390
...I received a tip telling me that we had a Matori in our midst.

12:31.390 --> 12:32.310
It wasn't just for me.

12:32.810 --> 12:35.020
It was addressed to all of our members.

12:35.020 --> 12:38.770
I found that wiretap in your room much earlier than that.

12:39.070 --> 12:40.860
I see.

12:40.860 --> 12:44.660
The guy must have panicked and set up a trap when he found out that I was after him.

12:51.000 --> 12:53.830
I'm the only one here risking my life for you.

12:54.750 --> 12:55.830
Don't forget that.

12:56.860 --> 12:58.040
Very well.

12:58.040 --> 12:59.250
I trust you.

13:08.510 --> 13:13.520
Director's Office

13:09.930 --> 13:10.930
Yes.

13:10.930 --> 13:12.350
I see.

13:12.350 --> 13:13.520
Yes, I understand.

13:13.850 --> 13:14.940
Thank you for your help.

13:21.070 --> 13:22.740
It was just as you suspected, Hiki.

13:23.240 --> 13:25.740
When I reviewed Kitagishi's past on the route that you indicated...

13:25.740 --> 13:28.700
...I learned that he used to be a drug planner who went under the name of Hatayama.

13:29.410 --> 13:31.540
A drug planner.

13:31.540 --> 13:35.410
A man with the ability to create blueprints on how to produce a drug.

13:35.410 --> 13:41.920
It's a major possibility that he used his position to import a large amount of plants from overseas to use as raw materials for the drug.

13:41.920 --> 13:43.170
It's all connected now.

13:44.340 --> 13:47.180
I just received a report from our expert substance analysts.

13:47.180 --> 13:51.680
They've determined that it is possible for the plant that Kai-kun brought back to be F.A.'s main ingredient.

13:52.010 --> 13:56.270
However, in order to make it, one would need the knowledge of a plant specialist and the use of high-quality facilities.

13:56.270 --> 13:56.940
What?

13:56.940 --> 13:58.350
I see.

13:58.350 --> 14:01.360
He must be making F.A. in the R&D lab.

14:01.360 --> 14:02.610
I can't say that for certain...

14:02.610 --> 14:05.570
...but it does act as a good pretext to connect this case to Kuzuya.

14:05.570 --> 14:06.530
Okay.

14:06.530 --> 14:11.660
I'll apply for a search warrant on Kitagishi,
and we'll raid those gardens within minutes.

14:11.660 --> 14:12.450
Director Hiki.

14:14.540 --> 14:17.290
I suggest that you hurry if you wish to act on time.

14:17.470 --> 14:20.710
This man who calls himself Kagura isn't trustworthy.

14:20.710 --> 14:22.000
What did you find?

14:22.000 --> 14:23.880
Well, to be more precise...

14:23.880 --> 14:25.550
...I <i>couldn't</i>  find anything.

14:25.550 --> 14:27.170
Akito Kagura.

14:27.170 --> 14:29.890
My information confirms that he is indeed a university student...

14:29.890 --> 14:33.720
...but just this summer, his family had declared him missing and asked the police to search for him.

14:33.720 --> 14:34.390
What?

14:34.720 --> 14:40.480
I found evidence that all data concerning his physical appearance was intentionally erased immediately afterwards.

14:40.480 --> 14:43.320
So, I had Miyoshi run over to check on the family...

14:43.650 --> 14:45.320
...but the house was burned to the ground...

14:45.320 --> 14:47.860
...and his family hasn't been seen ever since.

14:50.110 --> 14:50.820
Kaji-kun!

14:51.240 --> 14:52.030
You got it!

14:52.910 --> 14:54.740
I sense a strong force working behind the scenes.

15:10.630 --> 15:14.100
Closed Today

15:12.090 --> 15:14.100
T-The key...

15:14.470 --> 15:15.720
It's gone!

15:54.180 --> 15:54.930
This is...

15:55.510 --> 15:56.220
It's F.A.

16:02.020 --> 16:03.480
Kagura-san.

16:05.190 --> 16:07.020
F.A.

16:07.020 --> 16:09.650
The factory where Funny Angel is manufactured.

16:11.150 --> 16:13.410
I should thank you.

16:13.820 --> 16:16.990
I'd been looking for this.

16:18.700 --> 16:19.870
Thanks...

16:20.830 --> 16:22.080
...for finding it for me.

16:36.010 --> 16:37.640
Well, this is sudden.

16:37.640 --> 16:40.140
You've made me wait for this long and now you want it done tonight?

16:40.140 --> 16:41.890
I wanted to be certain that both of us were safe.

16:42.890 --> 16:45.440
By the way, was my advice useful to you?

16:45.440 --> 16:47.110
That was you?

16:47.610 --> 16:49.570
Consider it a Christmas present.

16:49.570 --> 16:50.820
It's all right.

16:50.980 --> 16:53.570
I'm searching for the traitor now in secret.

16:55.030 --> 16:56.570
That's good to hear.

16:57.030 --> 17:00.370
Well then, I look forward to meeting you.

17:00.660 --> 17:01.370
Yeah.

17:13.840 --> 17:16.300
My trade with Kotetsu will begin in two hours.

17:16.300 --> 17:18.100
I want you to come with me.

17:18.100 --> 17:21.600
Tell me if you think they are trustworthy or not.

17:21.600 --> 17:22.140
Okay.

17:40.950 --> 17:43.080
Have you managed to get in contact with Kitagishi?

17:43.080 --> 17:44.000
Not yet, sir.

17:44.330 --> 17:47.250
Where the hell did he disappear to at an important time like this?

17:53.550 --> 17:54.630
Sorry to keep you waiting.

17:57.050 --> 17:58.300
Are you Kotetsu?

17:58.300 --> 17:58.970
Yeah.

17:58.970 --> 18:01.560
How did you get in from the backyard?

18:01.560 --> 18:02.760
Who said you could?

18:02.760 --> 18:03.770
Well, I don't know.

18:03.770 --> 18:05.230
We were told to come in from here.

18:06.100 --> 18:07.440
Must have been Kitagishi.

18:07.440 --> 18:09.150
He's gone out of line.

18:09.150 --> 18:10.980
Let's start our transaction without delay.

18:10.980 --> 18:11.900
Before we do that...

18:46.270 --> 18:47.430
What's with the kid?

18:47.770 --> 18:49.190
He's a Matori officer.

18:49.190 --> 18:49.730
Matori?

18:51.780 --> 18:54.110
That's why I warned you, didn't I?

18:56.820 --> 18:59.400
"How much of a naïve sucker are you?"

18:59.400 --> 19:00.450
...was it?

19:00.450 --> 19:01.700
Because you really are.

19:16.510 --> 19:19.420
That Reiji-kun who you think is risking his life for you...

19:19.420 --> 19:21.180
...is really Hal Kurabayashi.

19:21.720 --> 19:23.050
He's one of the best Ma-to-ri around.

19:23.050 --> 19:23.640
He's one of the best Ma-to-ri around.

19:23.640 --> 19:24.220
He's one of the best Ma-to-ri around.

19:24.220 --> 19:25.060
He's one of the best Ma-to-ri around.

19:25.930 --> 19:27.390
You bastard!

19:28.140 --> 19:28.770
Don't fuck with me!

19:29.350 --> 19:31.100
Who's fucking around with who, now?

19:31.100 --> 19:35.150
You're the one who brought a Matori along with you for this important deal.

19:35.150 --> 19:36.980
Oh, right, sorry.

19:38.740 --> 19:40.990
This boy is a Matori, too, isn't he.

19:42.610 --> 19:44.870
He's quite amazing, you know.

19:44.870 --> 19:45.240
Look.

19:58.960 --> 19:59.840
Kitagishi-san...

20:02.260 --> 20:04.550
After all, in order to continue with his investigation,

20:04.550 --> 20:08.600
this boy killed him for being in the way and took the key to this room.

20:08.600 --> 20:09.520
No!

20:11.310 --> 20:13.100
A shame for you that he died.

20:13.100 --> 20:16.230
He was an excellent drug planner.

20:16.230 --> 20:18.820
Without him, you won't be able to supply F.A. to your clients.

20:19.020 --> 20:20.150
Bastard...

20:20.150 --> 20:22.950
What's more, the Reiji-kun that you put your full confidence in...

20:24.410 --> 20:26.370
...is lying Matori scum.

20:26.370 --> 20:26.870
Shut up!

20:27.370 --> 20:28.830
Enough of your bullshit.

20:28.830 --> 20:32.330
Or are you telling me that you know how to prove what you've just said?

20:33.580 --> 20:35.130
There is one way.

20:37.420 --> 20:38.250
Kuzuya-san.

20:39.710 --> 20:41.260
Let's make a bet.

20:41.260 --> 20:41.800
What?

20:42.340 --> 20:44.800
We'll make them shoot at each other.

20:46.800 --> 20:49.350
If Reiji-kun is the person you think he is...

20:49.350 --> 20:51.890
...then he should be able to get rid of one Matori nuisance.

20:52.640 --> 20:55.020
But if the two of them are pals...

20:58.520 --> 21:01.740
I bet on them not shooting, of course.

21:01.740 --> 21:04.030
They're partners, after all.

21:04.030 --> 21:05.490
What do you say?

21:08.240 --> 21:10.490
What are the conditions of the bet?

21:10.490 --> 21:13.870
If you win, we Kotetsu will affiliate under Asaya.

21:14.660 --> 21:17.670
I'll even provide you with guns and other weapons almost indefinitely...

21:17.670 --> 21:20.800
...and I guarantee full financial backing for all of your needs.

21:20.800 --> 21:21.550
What?

21:21.920 --> 21:24.300
But if I win...

21:24.300 --> 21:26.180
...everything in Asaya is mine.

21:38.730 --> 21:39.690
Very well.

21:39.690 --> 21:40.480
I accept.

21:46.570 --> 21:49.620
There's one bullet in each gun.

21:49.620 --> 21:53.080
If either of them die, you win.

22:05.970 --> 22:06.880
You can do it.

22:10.350 --> 22:12.260
Kill that boy with one clean shot.

22:28.410 --> 22:28.950
Well then...

22:29.490 --> 22:30.870
Let's begin.

22:32.030 --> 22:33.160
Showtime.

23:33.140 --> 23:35.180
If I told you to die...

23:35.180 --> 23:36.720
Would you die?

23:42.230 --> 23:43.100
Yes.

24:14.200 --> 24:15.220
My, my...

24:22.520 --> 24:23.900
You haven't changed a bit.

24:26.690 --> 24:29.940
Looks like I win the bet.

24:29.940 --> 24:30.280
No.

24:32.070 --> 24:33.240
It was I who won.

24:34.490 --> 24:35.530
Freeze!

24:35.530 --> 24:38.200
We're the Greater Kanto area's Narcotics Control Department!

24:41.410 --> 24:42.460
Sorry...

24:42.460 --> 24:44.330
...but Asaya belongs to me now.

24:52.050 --> 24:53.720
Don't let even one of them slip your fingers!

25:11.940 --> 25:12.900
You...

25:21.330 --> 25:22.870
This is... blood paste...

25:24.290 --> 25:27.080
That's quite a cheap life you risked for me.

25:27.250 --> 25:32.420
Sorry, but I don't have a life that's worthless enough to throw away for the likes of a drug dealer.

25:34.130 --> 25:35.180
I lose.

25:43.350 --> 25:44.430
You...

25:44.430 --> 25:45.230
Kagura!

25:52.940 --> 25:54.110
There's an underground tunnel!

26:00.870 --> 26:01.950
What?!

26:17.880 --> 26:18.680
Kagura!

26:19.090 --> 26:20.850
Throw down your weapon and turn yourself in!

26:30.860 --> 26:31.940
Kajiyama-san!

26:31.940 --> 26:32.940
What?

26:32.940 --> 26:34.400
We have a survivor!

26:34.400 --> 26:35.280
All right.

26:35.280 --> 26:35.940
Kagura!

26:36.530 --> 26:37.900
Don't move from there!

26:47.870 --> 26:48.330
Damn it...

26:49.870 --> 26:51.710
Kagura!!

27:08.060 --> 27:08.690
Hal...

27:16.780 --> 27:24.660
^onkei: think we need this one?

27:16.900 --> 27:24.700
Narcotics Control Department - Kanto-Shin'etsu Regional Bureau of Health and Welfare

27:18.150 --> 27:19.240
No good.

27:19.240 --> 27:21.780
The remaining Kotetsu member who survived...

27:21.780 --> 27:24.660
...is just a small-time hoodlum who was only gathered up for that day.

27:25.290 --> 27:28.660
None of the others were legitimate members either.

27:28.660 --> 27:29.710
Now I see what happened.

27:30.000 --> 27:31.000
What?

27:31.000 --> 27:33.420
There was no Kotetsu.

27:33.420 --> 27:34.130
What do you mean?

27:34.130 --> 27:39.550
Most likely, it's a fake organization that he made to take F.A. for himself and destroy Asaya.

27:39.550 --> 27:42.090
But that load of guns wasn't fake.

27:42.090 --> 27:48.020
Some other organization with the money to provide that,
did so in order to turn the lie into truth.

27:48.020 --> 27:50.520
No organization is able to do that.

27:50.520 --> 27:51.850
There is one.

27:51.850 --> 27:55.320
One that leaves no evidence or anything else indicating its existence behind.

27:55.320 --> 27:56.900
No evidence, huh?

27:56.900 --> 27:58.860
I've heard that description somewhere.

27:59.530 --> 28:02.700
The reason why he didn't let Hal-kun and Kai-kun use real guns...

28:02.700 --> 28:04.320
...was because he had no intention of killing them.

28:04.660 --> 28:05.870
No...

28:06.450 --> 28:09.290
Or is it because he needed to keep them alive...?

28:09.290 --> 28:09.910
Huh?

28:12.120 --> 28:13.040
It's nothing.

28:19.300 --> 28:22.510
Did you receive the data I got on F.A. manufacturing?

28:22.510 --> 28:23.010
Yeah.

28:24.340 --> 28:27.260
It's here along with a lovely bouquet.

28:27.260 --> 28:28.430
That's good.

28:28.850 --> 28:30.890
It turned out to be a good Christmas.

28:32.770 --> 28:35.480
Asaya has pretty good territory.

28:35.900 --> 28:37.900
We'll be able to sell three times more the drugs we're selling now.

28:38.110 --> 28:39.650
Yes.

28:39.650 --> 28:41.780
Everything is going according to plan.

28:41.780 --> 28:42.780
I see.

28:42.950 --> 28:45.910
Also, the key to Switch is as healthy as ever.

28:48.080 --> 28:49.740
You did well...

28:49.740 --> 28:50.750
...Akaha.

28:58.040 --> 29:00.170
Central General Hospital

28:59.800 --> 29:00.510
Hal!

29:00.510 --> 29:01.340
Let's go.

29:03.010 --> 29:03.970
You waited for me!

29:04.970 --> 29:06.800
There was simply no need to get checked at the hospital...

29:07.300 --> 29:08.300
Ouch, ouch!

29:08.300 --> 29:10.010
...just for a paintball!

29:10.010 --> 29:12.770
My head was right next to the muzzle, so it really was dangerous!

29:13.140 --> 29:14.020
Good grief.

29:14.020 --> 29:17.520
This wouldn't have happened if we'd just shot each other.

29:18.900 --> 29:19.820
No!

29:19.820 --> 29:21.530
What if those guns had been real?

29:21.530 --> 29:25.780
You should have been able to tell from the weight of the gun that it didn't hold real bullets.

29:25.780 --> 29:26.780
I still won't do it!

29:30.240 --> 29:31.080
I can't do it.

29:31.870 --> 29:34.040
Even if it was a bluff...

29:34.040 --> 29:35.540
...I could never shoot you!

29:38.750 --> 29:40.170
You're the worst.

29:45.550 --> 29:46.680
It's snowing.

29:57.440 --> 30:07.160
The pain comes back with every dawn.

30:10.580 --> 30:20.460
Again, another chapter of my dream fades.

30:24.090 --> 30:30.470
My distant memories are even now sealed anyway,

30:30.720 --> 30:36.810
For I see no need to find the key for its lock.

30:36.810 --> 30:43.190
I still have yet to see the hand.

30:43.440 --> 30:49.820
You still have yet to feel this hand.

30:49.990 --> 30:53.080
Now, without any hesitation,

30:53.330 --> 30:56.290
I simply wish to express this feeling

30:56.620 --> 31:02.210
In a way that it will reach you.

31:02.290 --> 31:09.680
Your Hand...
